      "requestAttempts": 1,
      "pronunciationText": "Now go across Period three, from sodium to chlorine. Each step adds one proton to the nucleus. The new electron goes into the same third shell, so the inner shells don't change, and there are still ten inner electrons. So the core charge climbs, from plus one for sodium to plus seven for chlorine. A stronger pull on the same shell draws the outer electrons closer, and the atom gets smaller.",
