      "pronunciationText": "Hang on, chlorine has more electrons. Shouldn't they take up more room? The extra electrons all go into the same outer shell, and electrons in the same shell barely shield each other. So the nucleus's extra pull wins. More electrons in the same shell doesn't mean a bigger atom.",
