      "requestAttempts": 1,
      "pronunciationText": "Potassium. Going down Group one, each element has one more occupied shell than the one above, so its outer electron sits further from the nucleus. Yes, potassium has more protons, but it also has more inner electrons shielding them. Its core charge is nineteen minus eighteen, plus one, the same as lithium's. With the same core charge, the extra shell wins. So atomic radius increases down a group.",
