      "pronunciationText": "In an exam, don't just say the atom gets smaller. Name the cause. Across a period, the number of protons increases while electrons go into the same shell, so the stronger effective nuclear charge pulls the outer electrons closer. Down a group, each element has an extra occupied shell, so the outer electrons are further from the nucleus.",
